{{Opinion polling for Brazilian presidential elections}}
Since the [[2022 Brazilian general election]], polling companies have published surveys tracking national voting intention for the [[2026 Brazilian general election]]. The results of these surveys are listed below in reverse chronological order, and include candidates who frequently polled above 3% and are [[List of political parties in Brazil|registered in a party]], as well as eligible by the [[Superior Electoral Court]] of Brazil. They also include candidates from parties that passed the [[electoral threshold]]{{efn|name="electoral threshold"}} in 2022, and therefore have access to public campaign funding, free radio and television advertising time, and the right to participate in debates.

== First round ==

=== Graphical summary ===
[[Aggregate data]] of voting intention from opinion polling for the presidential election. Each line represents a [[local regression]]. Only prospective candidates and individuals who frequently appear in polls are included. The "Undecided", "Blank/Null" and "Absent" groups were calculated out.[[File:2026 brazilian presidential election polls.svg|center|920px]]

