{{efn|name="electoral threshold"
|The electoral threshold in 2022 required each party to obtain at least 2% of the valid votes for the Chamber of Deputies nationwide, with a minimum of 1% in one-third of the states (nine states), or to elect at least 11 federal deputies distributed across nine states.
}}

{{efn|name="others candidates final"
|So far, the candidates who have neither reached at least 3% in recent polls nor are affiliated with parties that passed the electoral threshold in 2022 are as follows:
* Clariana Barão ([[Christian Democracy (Brazil)|DC]])
* [[Edmilson Costa]] ([[Brazilian Communist Party|PCB]])
* [[Hertz Dias]] ([[United Socialist Workers' Party|PSTU]])
* [[Pablo Marçal]] ([[PRTB]]) ''(ineligible)''
* [[Rui Costa Pimenta]] ([[Workers' Cause Party|PCO]])
* [[Samara Martins]] ([[Popular Unity (Brazil)|UP]])
* Wilson Grassi ([[Democrat (Brazil)|Democrat]])
}}

{{efn|name="STF crisis"
|The STF crisis intensified on 1 September, with the revelation of messages exchanged between Justice [[Alexandre de Moraes]] and banker [[Daniel Vorcaro]] — including on the day of his arrest — whose confidentiality had been lifted by Justice [[André Mendonça]]. The messages revealed indications of improper closeness between the two, along with other revelations involving Prosecutor General [[Paulo Gonet]]. In response, on 3 September, Moraes requested that an investigation be opened against Mendonça as part of the [[Inquiry 4781|Fake News Inquiry]], for his handling of the [[Banco Master scandal|Master case investigation]].<br/><br/>
The situation escalated on 8 September, when Mendonça ordered the preventive removal of the Federal Police's Director-General, [[Andrei Rodrigues]], alleging that he had been illegally monitored by the PF. The following day, 9 September, Justice [[Flávio Dino]] ordered the immediate reinstatement of Rodrigues, creating a standoff. Later that same day, the Court's president, Justice [[Edson Fachin]], suspended both Mendonça's decision and Dino's, maintaining the status quo until a final ruling, and removed Moraes as rapporteur of the fake news inquiry, taking over the case himself. Fachin also called an extraordinary session for 15 September, at which the full court is expected to rule on the legality of Mendonça's actions, the validity of the evidence obtained from Vorcaro's phone, and the Prosecutor General's Office's request to annul the entire procedure.
}}

{{efn|name="Free airtime"
|Candidates from coalitions that include parties which passed the electoral threshold in 2022 are entitled to free advertisement on television and radio from 28 August to 1 October 2026. The block for presidential candidates occurs three days per week, twice per day, for 12min30s, of which 10% are divided equally among all candidates entitled to airtime, and 90% are distributed proportionally to the number of federal deputies of the parties in each candidate's coalition.<ref name=airtime1>{{cite web |url=https://www.tse.jus.br/legislacao/compilada/res/2019/resolucao-no-23-610-de-18-de-dezembro-de-2019 |title=Resolution no. 23610, of 18 December 2019 |publisher=Superior Electoral Court of Brazil |language=pt |access-date=16 May 2026 |archive-date=1 April 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20220401014531/https://www.tse.jus.br/legislacao/compilada/res/2019/resolucao-no-23-610-de-18-de-dezembro-de-2019 |url-status=live }}</ref><br><br>The candidates entitled to free TV and radio airtime are as follows:
* Lula: 5min32s
* F. Bolsonaro: 4min20s
* Caiado: 2min02s
* Cury: 36s
}}

