{{efn|name="party conventions"
|The period for party conventions runs from 20 July to 5 August. During this period, all political parties must formally nominate their candidates for every office they intend to contest. The deadline for registering candidates with the Superior Electoral Court is 15 August.
}}

{{efn|name="Aécio Neves"
|This scenario included [[Aécio Neves]] ([[PSDB]]), who had not announced his candidacy but had been the subject of speculation.
}}

{{efn|name="Banco Master"
|Messages and audio recordings released by the press show that Flávio Bolsonaro negotiated US$24 million (R$134 million) directly with [[Daniel Vorcaro]], former owner of Banco Master and central figure in the scandal. The money was allegedly intended to finance the film [[Dark Horse (2026 film)|Dark Horse]], about [[Jair Bolsonaro 2018 presidential campaign]]. <br/><br/> Documents show that at least US$10.6 million (R$61 million) was paid between February and May 2025 in six bank transfers. Analysis of the messages shows that part of the payments were made by Daniel Vorcaro to the Havengate Development Fund LP, based in Texas and linked to a lawyer for the Bolsonaro family.
}}

{{efn|name="Ciro Gomes"
|This scenario included [[Ciro Gomes]] ([[PSDB]]), who had not announced his candidacy but had been the subject of speculation.
}}

{{efn|name="descompatibilização" 
|According to Brazilian electoral law, members of the executive branch (such as mayors, governors, and cabinet ministers) must leave office up to six months before the election if they intend to run for another position (except when seeking reelection).
}}

{{efn|name="tarcísio" 
|Tarcísio de Freitas remained in office as governor in order to run for reelection. As a result, he is legally barred from running for president in 2026.
}}

